   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"2\\left( {x + 6} \\right) = 3x + 4 - \\left( {x + 5} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Simplify each side as much as possible.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x + 12 = 3x + 4 - x - 5\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x + 12 = 2x - 1\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Collect the variable terms on one side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x + 12 - 2x = 2x - 1 - 2x\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"12 =  - 1\"></span></p>\n<p>This is a false statement, so this equation has no solution.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"12 =  - 1\">12 =  - 1</span>, which is false; therefore, this is a false statement, and the equation has no solution."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
